ndards?\n\nResponse A:\nThere is no single recommended cadence, as the frequency must be tailored to the specific volatility of each jurisdiction's legal landscape and the complexity of your contract mix. You should likely run the regression quarterly to capture emerging regulatory changes while performing ad-hoc stress tests whenever a major limitation-of-liability standard shifts in a key market.\n\nResponse B:\nThere is no single recommended cadence, as the frequency must be tailored to the specific volatility of each jurisdiction's legal landscape and the complexity of your contract mix. You should likely run a quarterly review to capture emerging case law changes, followed by an annual deep-dive to reconcile conflicting limitation-of-liability standards across your portfolio.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-002", "question_number": 2, "request_key": "cfa0cb5043ec869c9a99c97246406