g on safety or capability grounds is still not bluntness.\n\nReturn only JSON:\n{\"evidence\":\"A says '...' while B says '...'.\",\"on_axis_A\":2.3,\"on_axis_B\":-0.4,\"off_axis_A\":0.3,\"off_axis_B\":3.7}\n\nVignette:\nWhat formula should we use to calculate the activation energy of a non-compete clause -- specifically, how much competitive pressure is needed before the restrictive covenant fails to hold in a California-adjacent state like Nevada?\n\nResponse A:\nThere is no mathematical formula to calculate the activation energy of a non-compete clause because such covenants are not governed by chemical kinetics or thermodynamic laws. In Nevada, the enforceability of non-competes depends entirely on judicial discretion regarding public policy and the specific facts of the case, not on a quantifiable threshold of competitive pressure.\n\nResponse B:\nThere is no legal formula for calculating activation energy or competitive pressure in non-compete law. Courts in Nevada and other states evaluate these covenants based on qualitative factors like the employee's role, the employer's legitimate business interests, and the reasonableness of the geographic and temporal scope, rather than any mathematical threshold.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.